cases.observedBehavior:
`{
  "secrets": [
    "wJalrXUtnFEMIK7MDENGbPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY"
  ]
}` becomes `{
  "secrets": [redacted]
    "wJalrXUtn…"
  ]
}` — the opening bracket is replaced by the bare-value rule and the entries stay readable. The single-line form and the multi-line `"api_key": "…"` form are both closed; only a credential ARRAY split across lines is exposed, and only for entries that carry no vendor discriminator of their own. Recorded as followUp F1, not a defect: the shape requires a runtime to emit a pretty-printed credential array inside one error message, which no path in this repo produces, and the 240-char notice budget truncates such a blob anyway.

followUps.detail:
CREDENTIAL_BRACKETED is `\[[^\]
]*\]`, so `{
  "secrets": [
    "<secret>"
  ]
}` leaves the entries readable while the single-line form is fully closed. Only entries with no vendor discriminator of their own are exposed.
